    "lawCode": "Add §13-633, NYC Ad Cd",
    "lawSection": "New York City Administrative Code",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6988\n\nSPONSOR: JACKSON\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in\nrelation to granting members of the city's police force eligibility for\nretirement and pension based on previous service as traffic enforcement\nagents\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nProvides New York City Police Officers who previously served as traffic\nenforcement officers with pension credit for their years of prior\nservice.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the administrative code of the City of New York by\nadding a new section 13-633 to provide that time served as a member of\nthe city's traffic enforcement bureau who subsequently became an NYPD\nofficer, to have their prior service time included and counted for\npurposes of calculating their pension.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCertain persons who served in various public service capacities prior to\nbecoming an NYPD officer receive credit for their prior service, such as\nthose who were formerly school safety officers. This bill would create\nparity for those who formerly served as traffic enforcement officers.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2023-2024: S.5478 - Reported and Committed to Civil Service and\nPensions/A.3129 - Referred to Governmental Employees\n\n2021-2022: S.9286 - Referred to Cities 1/A.10611Referred to Governmental\nEmployees\n\n \nSTATE AND LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
